  "summary": "Policarpa Salavarrieta, known as La Pola, was a seamstress who passed information from royalist households in Bogotá to rebels during Colombia's independence struggle. Captured and condemned for espionage, she was executed in Bogotá on 14 November 1817; her birth year and place remain uncertain.",
